---
import BaseHead from '@components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '@components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '@components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '@/consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Certified Trackerless Web-Burger" description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main class="grid-layout flow">
      <img
        src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6650f9fc-80d0-4169-8a86-25e53e24109f"
        alt=""
        class="image-accent"
        width="192"
        height="171"
      />

      <section class="">
        <h1>Certified Trackerless Web-Burger</h1>
        <p class="wrap-balance">
          This website is a guaranteed 100% trackerless, free-range, web burger.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr />

      <article class="flow">
        <p>
          <strong>No trackers? How will you know who visits your site?</strong>
        </p>
        <p>I won't! But hey, YOU'RE here...</p>
        <p>
          I <em>do</em> load JavaScript on these pages, but it's the JavaScript
          I <em>want</em> to send for you. For funsies, not for tracking.
        </p>
        <hr />
        <p>
          <strong>
            But how will you know what content is performing well?
          </strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          I won't! But in a way, that's freeing because{' '}
          <a href="https://adactio.com/journal/20996">I publish for myself</a>.
          If someone is helped by something I wrote, I hope they will reach out
          like the beautiful 100% human-being they are and let me know.
        </p>
        <p class="flow-2">
          <small>
            Dancing burger animation by{' '}
            <a href="https://giphy.com/stickers/food-hungry-burger-2NcM1fPMZ5EWDh694K">
              Alex Bradt
            </a>
          </small>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .image-accent {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 12rem;
  }
</style>
